=> df means Disk Free.

It tells you how much disk space is available and how much is being used.

=> Basic command
df

Usually, we use:

df -h

-h means human-readable, so sizes are shown as GB, MB, etc.

=> Example:

Filesystem      Size  Used Avail Use% Mounted on
/dev/sda1        50G   30G   18G  63% /

=> Meaning:

Size → Total disk space = 50 GB
Used → Used space = 30 GB
Avail → Available space = 18 GB
Use% → 63% used
/ → Root filesystem
Very common admin command
df -h

You use this when someone says:

"Server disk is getting full."
